<!--
    The same PiKit wordmark, inked black for the white icon the personalization
    page offers (`LauncherIcon.LIGHT`). The path data and fillType are
    `ic_launcher_foreground`'s character for character, and the fill colour is the
    only difference.

    A second copy is a thing that drifts, so the copy is checked rather than
    trusted: `tools/render-icon.py` reads both files, compares their path data
    and fillType, and fails the build when they disagree. A glyph that was edited
    in one of them and not the other is two icons that are not the same mark, and
    it is exactly the kind of change nobody re-reads this comment to remember.

    No `<monochrome>` of its own: the themed-icon layer is recoloured by the
    system, so the black icon and the white icon share `ic_launcher_monochrome`.
-->
